<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img class="phero-img" src="/assets/img/photos/hartford-office-tower.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hartford-office-tower-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hartford-office-tower.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="1800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/ct-appraisal-services/">Services</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</span></nav><p class="kicker kicker-light">Appraisal service</p><h1>Commercial, Condo Association and HOA Insurance Appraisal in Connecticut</h1><p class="phero-lede">Larger buildings bring larger gaps: flat roofs measured in tens of thousands of square feet, multi-building associations and converted mills with layered construction. We bring the documentation those claims demand.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/contact-ct-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Property types</dt><dd>Office · retail · HOA · mill</dd></div><div><dt>Roofs</dt><dd>TPO · EPDM · BUR · metal</dd></div><div><dt>Approach</dt><dd>Building-by-building</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>The commercial claims we value</h2>
<ul>
<li>Office and medical buildings in Stamford, Hartford and the I-91 corridor</li>
<li>Strip centers and freestanding retail</li>
<li>Converted brick mills in the Naugatuck Valley and eastern Connecticut</li>
<li>Condominium associations with dozens of buildings and shared roofs</li>
<li>Houses of worship, private schools and nonprofits</li>
<li>Mixed-use buildings with storefronts below and apartments above</li>
</ul>
<h2>Why commercial appraisals need more structure</h2>
<p>Commercial policies often include coinsurance clauses, scheduled limits, ordinance-or-law coverage and business income components that change how a loss is valued and paid. A good valuation separates each building and each coverage part so the panel can see exactly what is being decided.</p>
<h3>Low-slope roofing</h3>
<p>Flat and low-slope roofs are common on Connecticut commercial buildings. Disputes usually turn on whether a membrane is repairable, how much insulation is wet, and whether code requires added insulation when the roof is replaced. We document core samples and moisture surveys where needed.</p>
<h3>Associations and boards</h3>
<p>For condo associations and HOAs, we coordinate with the board and property manager, keep reporting consistent across buildings, and explain the process in language that works for an owners’ meeting.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Coverage questions come first</b>If the carrier disputes coverage for part of the loss, such as wear and tear on an older roof, that issue may need to be addressed separately from appraisal. We will tell you where the line sits.</div>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can appraisal include business income?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Some policies allow it if the dispute is over the amount of the business income loss. It depends on the policy wording, and accounting support is usually needed.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work with association boards?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We report to the board or its designee, attend meetings when helpful and keep documentation organized building by building.</p></div></details><details><summary>What about coinsurance?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A coinsurance clause can reduce payment if the property was underinsured. We flag the issue early so it can be addressed with your broker or an attorney.</p></div></details></div>
<h2>Related services</h2><div class="related"><a href="/ct-appraisal-services/roof-and-hail-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/ct-appraisal-services/wind-and-tornado-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/ct-appraisal-services/hurricane-and-tropical-storm-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Hurricane &amp; Tropical Storm Appraisal</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div>
